A: with h(formula) = 1, h(term) = 0.05: rho = 0.750 < 1 for every type (law depends on k only through [k = 0]); note every formula production has >= 1 child, as the referee says, yet the criterion holds
B: root sort formula, 200000 draws: mean size 14.621 (s.e. 0.038); Lemma 1.6 bound 80.0; P(size >= L) for L = 10, 20, 40, 80: 4.57e-01, 2.18e-01, 7.20e-02, 1.29e-02
   empirical log-tail decay per node between L = 20 and 40: 0.055 nats
B: root sort term, 200000 draws: mean size 4.016 (s.e. 0.015); Lemma 1.6 bound 4.0; P(size >= L) for L = 10, 20, 40, 80: 9.92e-02, 3.23e-02, 6.50e-03, 5.65e-04
   empirical log-tail decay per node between L = 20 and 40: 0.080 nats
B: for a term root at k = 0 the exact mean is 1/(1 - 0.75) = 4, equal to the bound (single-type case, where the bound is tight)
C: rho = 0.9: any admissible h has h(k)/h(0) <= 6.39e-01 (k = 10), 5.26e-05 (k = 100), 3.49e-46 (k = 1000), 6.11e-92 (k = 2000)  -> 0, so no h_min > 0 exists
C: rho = 0.99: any admissible h has h(k)/h(0) <= 1.66e+00 (k = 10), 7.25e-01 (k = 100), 8.63e-05 (k = 1000), 3.73e-09 (k = 2000)  -> 0, so no h_min > 0 exists
C: rho = 0.999: any admissible h has h(k)/h(0) <= 1.82e+00 (k = 10), 1.79e+00 (k = 100), 7.35e-01 (k = 1000), 2.70e-01 (k = 2000)  -> 0, so no h_min > 0 exists
C: the referee's chain (per-type mean 1 - 1/(k+2)^2 < 1, infinite with probability 1/2) is excluded by the revised definition.
